sections.content:
Without generics, you'd need separate functions for each type:

```bpl
frame maxInt(a: int, b: int) ret int { ... }
frame maxFloat(a: float, b: float) ret float { ... }
frame maxString(a: string, b: string) ret string { ... }
```

With generics, write it **once**:

```bpl
frame max<T>(a: T, b: T) ret T { ... }
```

The compiler generates specialized code for each type used. This is called **monomorphization** - zero runtime cost!

